# The index write gives a slot another address only after the field's admission (the book, structure-index): a slot
# that holds a Structure refuses the address of an int cell.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
int: j 40
sub: main () (
    S:
        int: a 1
        N: (int: x 7)
)
    S[1] := @j
main()
